---
layout: base.njk
modelLinks:
  - [Docs, 'https://docs.stisim.org']
  - [Tutorials, 'https://docs.stisim.org/tutorials']
  - [Examples gallery, 'https://docs.stisim.org/examples/']
  - [Roadmap, 'https://github.com/orgs/starsimhub/projects/26']
filters:
  - [all, All]
  - [published, Published]
  - [in-flight, In flight]
  - [dashboard, Live dashboards]
---
{% from "components.njk" import spectrum, studyCard %}

<section id="model" class="hero">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">Agent-based STI + HIV modeling · Built on Starsim</p>
    <h1>STIsim</h1>
    <p class="lede">
STIsim is an agent-based modeling framework for simulating co-circulating sexually transmitted infections. Built on the Starsim architecture, it supports structured sexual networks, multiple co-transmitting infections (HIV, syphilis, chlamydia, gonorrhea, trichomoniasis, bacterial vaginosis, and others), risk-stratified populations, and a flexible intervention library spanning screening, testing, treatment, and prevention. It is implemented in pure Python, extensively tested and documented, and runs in seconds to minutes on a laptop.
    </p>
    <div class="installs">
      <div class="inst">
        <span class="lbl">Installation</span>
        <code>pip install stisim</code>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="links">
      {% for link in modelLinks %}
      <a href="{{ link[1] }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">{{ link[0] }} <i>↗</i></a>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="research" class="sec">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="kicker">Research</p>
    <p class="sub">What has been done with the model, and what is under way.</p>
    <div class="chips" role="tablist">
      {% for f in filters %}
      <button class="chip{{ ' on' if loop.first }}" data-f="{{ f[0] }}">{{ f[1] }}</button>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      {% for study in collections.studies %}{{ studyCard(study) }}{% endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
